{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>I have set you as Elohim to Pharaoh.</b> A judge and ruler — to subdue him with plagues and chastisements." "<b>shall be your prophet.</b> As its Targum renders — \"your interpreter.\" And so every term of prophecy is a man who proclaims and makes heard to the people words of reproof, and it is from the root of ״נִיב שְׂפָתַיִם״ (Isaiah 57), ״יָנוּב חָכְמָה״ (Proverbs 10), ״וַיְכַל מֵהִתְנַבֵּאת״ of Samuel (I 10); and בְּלַעַז they call him פרידיכ״ר."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {1 "the la'az פרידיכ״ר is Old French preeschier/predicator, 'preacher'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:55.911701246Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}